# Constellation labels — zero Mesh raycasts on terrain

Burned on 2026-11-14 (`d1699d4`): night immersive froze (~1 frame / tens of seconds)
because HTML constellation names called `Raycaster.intersectObjects` on the full
near/far DEM every frame (~86 labels × millions of tris). Day was fine; night died.

## Forbidden

| Hack | Symptom |
|---|---|
| `Raycaster.intersectObjects(terrainRoot, true)` (near/far/LOD meshes) | Night-only freeze / multi-second frames |
| Any per-frame Mesh raycast / BVH query against immersive terrain for sky labels | Same — feature is secondary, app must stay interactive |
| “Just for labels behind ridges” framing that reintroduces mesh picks | Already burned — do not restore |

## Allowed (locked baseline)

- Height-field samples along the sightline (`groundYAt` / DEM elev), O(1) steps
- Horizon cut (`dir.y` threshold) without touching meshes
- If occlusion is too wrong or still costly: **hide the feature** (turn labels off) — never trade frame time for ridge hiding

## Rule of landing

A constellation / night-sky “fix” that makes night pan worse than HEAD is a failed
change — revert immediately. Do not reintroduce mesh picking for this secondary UI.
